    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "1: Can I wear braces with missing back molars? Yes. We stabilise the arch, hold or close spaces as needed, then plan dental implants or partial dentures once the bite settles and positions are ideal. 2: Do I need implants before braces or after? Often after. Alignment first sets exact spacing. Then implants go where bone and symmetry are best. Some cases stage one implant earlier for chewing stability. 3: Which braces are best if I’m missing teeth? Fixed metal braces give strong control for complex moves. Clear aligners work for moderate changes. Choice depends on your orthodontist, space size, and goals. 4: Can braces close gaps from old tooth loss completely? Sometimes. Small spaces can close cleanly. Larger gaps can sometimes be closed, but are usually preserved for tooth replacement so the bite and midline remain balanced and stable for the long term. 5: What should I watch during treatment? Keep gums and teeth clean, prevent tooth decay, and commit to regular checkups. We adjust forces so surrounding teeth stay upright and your final spacing looks natural."
    }
